.SH NAME
ICC - Driver for compiling, assembling, and linking C programs for the iPSC/860\& system.
.\" End Summary
.SH SYNOPSIS 
.br
\&\fBicc\fR\fR\& [\fR\fIswitches\fI\fR\&] \fR\fIsourcefile\fI\fR\
\&... 
.SH DESCRIPTION 
.LP
The\fB\& icc\fR\fR\& command invokes the iPSC/860\& C compiler, assembler, and linker with switches derived \
from the driver's command line arguments. 
.LP
The\fB\& icc\fR\fR\& bases its processing on the suffixes of the files it is passed: 
.IP "\(bu" 0.2i
Files whose names end with ``.c'' are considered to be C programs. They are preprocessed, \
compiled, and assembled. The resulting object file is placed in the current directory. 
.IP "\(bu" 0.2i
Files whose names end with ``.s'' are considered to be i860 assembly language files. They are \
assembled and the resulting object file is placed in the current directory. 
.IP "\(bu" 0.2i
Files whose names end with ``.o'' are considered to be object files. They are passed directly to \
the linker if linking is requested. 
.IP "\(bu" 0.2i
Files whose names end with ``.a'' are considered to be \fBar\fR\fR\
\& libraries. No action is performed on \&``.a'' files unless linking is requested. 
.IP "\(bu" 0.2i
All other files are taken as object files and passed to the linker (if linking is requested) with a \
warning message.
.LP
If a single C program is compiled and linked with one \fBicc\fR\fR\
\& command, then the intermediate object and assembly files are deleted. 
.LP
The compiler is targeted to the Intel i860 System Binary Standard (SBS) for the Intel APX system. \
The compiler creates object files and executables that will function for any system conforming to the \
SBS. In addition, the compiler can create object files that will work for any system conforming to \
the System V, Release 4 Application Binary Interface (ABI) for the i860 microprocessor. 
.SH SWITCHES 
.LP
When debug or profile objects are compiled using the \fB\&-g\fR\fR\
\& or \fB\&-p\fR\fR\& switches, respectively, the same switch should be used when using \fB\
icc\fR\fR\& to link the objects. 
.ta 1.2i 5.9i
.HP 1.2i
\fB\&-node\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Creates executable program for RX node (default). 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 5.9i
.HP 1.2i
