\fBextract=\fR\fR\&[\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\&[\fB\&,\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\
\&...]] 
.br
Pass options to the function extractor. The \fB\&-o\fR\fIfile\fI\fR\
\& option must be used with this switch to tell the compiler \
where to place the extracted functions. The library name must contain a period. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fR\fIfunction\(em\fI\fRA non-numeric option not containing a \
period is assumed to be a function name. The named function is extracted. 
.RE
