\fBperf\fR\fR\&[\fB\&=\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\&[\fB\&,\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\
\&...]] 
.br
Generate instrumentation code for PAT (the iPSC/860\& Parallel Performance Analysis Tools). If no \fR\fI\
option\fI\fRs are specified, then all PAT instrumentation is enabled \
and all performance monitoring is performed automatically. The available \fR\fI\
option\fI\fRs are:
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBauto\fR\fR\(emPerform performance monitoring automatically.
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBmanual\fR\fR\(emPerform performance monitoring only when requested by calls to the PAT library.
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBprof\fR\fR\&[\fB\&=\fR\fR\&{ \fBauto\fR\fR\& | \fBmanual\fR\fR\
\& }]\(emEnable execution profiling (automatically or manually, default \fB\
\&=auto\fR\fR\&).
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBcomm\fR\fR\&[\fB\&=\fR\fR\&{ \fBauto\fR\fR\& | \fBmanual\fR\fR\
\& }]\(emEnable communication tracing (automatically or manually, default \fB\
\&=auto\fR\fR\&).
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBevent\fR\fR\&[\fB\&=\fR\fR\&{ \fBauto\fR\fR\& | \fBmanual\fR\fR\
\& }]\(emEnable event tracing \&(automatically or manually, default \fB\
\&=auto\fR\fR\&).
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
See the \fR\fIiPSC\*R/860\fI\fR\fR\fR\fR\fR\fR\fI\& Parallel Performance Analysis \
Tools Manual\fI\fR\& for complete information on PAT.
.RE
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fBquad\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Force top-level objects (e.g., local arrays, structures, \
etc.) of size greater than or equal to 16 bytes to be quad-aligned. Note that this does not affect items \
within a top-level object; such items are quad-aligned only if appropriate padding is inserted.\
\& 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\&[\fBno\fR\fR\&]\fBreentrant\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' \&[Don't] enable optimizations that may result in code \
that is not reentrant (default \fB\&-Mnoreentrant\fR\fR\&). Even \
with \fB\&-Mreentrant\fR\fR\&, the code may still not be reentrant \
if it is improperly written (e.g., declares static variables). 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fBsafeptr=\fR\fR\&[\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\&[\fB\&,\fR\fIoption\fI\fR\
\&...]] 
.br
Override data dependence between C pointers and arrays. This is a potentially very dangerous option \
since the potential exists for code to be generated that will result in unexpected or incorrect results as is \
defined by ANSI C. However, when used properly, this option has the potential to greatly enhance the \
performance of code, especially floating point oriented loops. Combinations of the \fR\fI\
options\fI\fR\& may be used and interact appropriately. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBdummy\fR\fR\& or \fBarg\fR\fR\(emC dummy arguments (pointers and \
arrays) are treated with the same copyin/copyout semantics as Fortran dummy arguments. 
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBauto\fR\fR\(emC local or \fBauto\fR\fR\& variables (pointers and arrays) \
are assumed not to overlap or conflict with each other and are independent. 
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBstatic\fR\fR\(emC \fBstatic\fR\fR\& variables (pointers and arrays) are \
assumed not to overlap or conflict with each other and are independent. 
.RE
.RS 2.4i
.LP
\fBglobal\fR\fR\(emC global or \fBextern\fR\fR\& variables (pointers and \
arrays) are assumed not to overlap or conflict with each other and are independent. 
.RE
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\&[\fBno\fR\fR\&]\fBsignextend\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' \&[Don't] sign extend when a narrowing conversion \
overflows (default \fB\&-Msignextend\fR\fR\&). For example, if \fB\
\&-Msignextend\fR\fR\& is in effect and an integer containing \
the value 65535 is converted to a \fBshort\fR\fR\&, the value of \
the \fBshort\fR\fR\& will be -1. This option is provided for \
compatibility with other compilers, even though ANSI C specifies that the result of such conversions are \
undefined. \fB\&-Msignextend\fR\fR\& will decrease performance \
on such conversions. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\&[\fBno\fR\fR\&]\fBsingle\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' \&[Don't] suppress the ANSI-specified conversion of \fB\
float\fR\fR\& to \fBdouble\fR\fR\& when passing arguments to a function \
with no prototype in scope (default \fB\&-Mnosingle\fR\fR\&). \fB\
\&-Msingle\fR\fR\& may result in faster code when single precision is used a lot, but is non-ANSI compliant. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\&[\fBno\fR\fR\&]\fBstreamall\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' \&[Don't] stream all vectors to and from cache in a vector \
loop (default \fB\&-Mstreamall\fR\fR\&). When \fB\&-Mnostreamall\fR\fR\
\& is in effect, the compiler chooses one vector to come directly from or go directly to main memory, without \
being streamed into or out of cache. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fBstride0\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Emit correct code for vectors with a stride (loop \
increment) of 0, no matter what the optimization or vectorization level.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
