\fR\fR\&0\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' A basic block is generated for each C statement. No \
scheduling is done between statements. No global optimizations are performed. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fR\fR\&1\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' Scheduling within extended basic blocks is performed. \
Some register allocation is performed. No global optimizations are performed. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fR\fR\&2\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' All level 1 optimizations are performed. In addition, \
traditional scalar optimizations such as induction recognition and loop invariant motion are performed \
by the global optimizer. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fR\fR\&3\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' All level 2 optimizations are performed. In addition, \
software pipelining is performed.
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.ta 1.2i 4.7i
.RS 1.2i
.HP 1.2i
\fR\fR\&4\fR\fR\& 	\h'-\w' 'u' All level 3 optimizations are performed, but with more \
aggressive register allocation for software pipelined loops. In addition, code for pipelined loops is \
scheduled several ways, with the best way selected for the assembly file. 
.RE
.ta 0.50i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i +0.5i
.RS 1.2i
.LP
If a \fR\fIlevel\fI\fR\& is not supplied with \fB\&-O\fR\fR\& then the optimization level is set to \fR\fR\
\&2\fR\fR\&. If \fB\&-O\fR\fR\& is not specified, then the default level is \fR\fR\
\&0\fR\fR\& if \fB\&-g\fR\fR\& is specified, and \fR\fR\&1\fR\fR\
\& if \fB\&-g\fR\fR\& is not specified. 
.RE
.ta 1.2i 5.9i
